      summary: "A young person detained in custody in relation to proceedings must be held in a safe, fair and humane manner in a designated place of temporary detention, and may be held under a peace officer's supervision during transfer to and from court. The young person must be held separate from adults unless a judge or justice is satisfied that, in the young person's best interests, they cannot safely be held in a youth facility or none is available within a reasonable distance. After the young person turns 18, the court may on the provincial director's application authorize temporary detention in an adult provincial facility if in their best interests or the public interest, and a young person who is 20 or older when detention begins is held in an adult provincial facility. The provincial director may transfer a young person between places of temporary detention, and a young person restrained by a peace officer after arrest must be moved to a place of temporary detention at the first reasonable opportunity after appearing before a judge or justice under s. 503 of the Criminal Code.",
