      maxPenalty: "",
      summary: "A young person against whom an information or indictment is laid must first appear before a youth justice court judge or justice, who must have the charge read, tell an unrepresented young person of the right to counsel, and, where notice of intention to seek an adult sentence was given or s. 16 applies, tell them the court might impose an adult sentence on a finding of guilt. Waiver is possible if counsel advises the young person has been informed. If unrepresented, the court must also, before accepting a plea, be satisfied the young person understands the charge, explain adult sentence consequences if applicable, explain the election of mode of trial where it applies, and explain the choice of pleas. If the court is not satisfied the young person understands the charge, it enters a not guilty plea and proceeds to trial (unless an election must be put), and if not satisfied they understand the other matters, it directs that they be represented by counsel.",
