      severity: "",
      maxPenalty: "",
      summary: "At least one month before the custodial portion of a s. 42(2)(o), (q) or (r) sentence ends, the provincial director must bring the young person before the youth justice court, which sets the conditions of conditional supervision after hearing the young person. The order must include conditions including keeping the peace and being of good behaviour, appearing in court when required, reporting to the provincial director on release, telling the provincial director immediately of arrest or police questioning, reporting to police or a named person as instructed, advising the provincial director of address and changes, not possessing weapons, ammunition, prohibited devices or explosive substances except as authorized, and complying with reasonable instructions to prevent a breach or protect society. The court may add conditions such as travelling directly to the place of residence on release, making reasonable efforts to obtain and keep employment, attending school or a suitable program, and residing with a parent or other suitable adult.",
