      summary: "A person covered by s. 159 who is found guilty, other than someone convicted in ordinary court as defined in the Young Offenders Act, is sentenced under this Act, except that s. 42(2)(r) applies only with the young person's consent. A young person being sentenced under this Act while subject to a disposition under s. 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act may, on application of the Attorney General or the young person, have the remaining portion of that disposition treated for all purposes as if it were a sentence under s. 42(2)(n) or (q), unless that would bring the administration of justice into disrepute. For s. 94 reviews, the relevant date is the day the disposition came into force under the Young Offenders Act.",
